<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec_v-to-e" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
	<title>Finding E from V</title>

		<activity>
      <title>Warm-Up</title>
      <p></p>
			<p>Starting with what you learned about <xref ref="e_to_v"/>: suppose you instead knew the electric potential <m>V</m> and you want to figure out the electric field <m>\vec{E}</m>. What mathematical operation could you perform on <m>V</m> to get <m>\vec{E}</m>?</p>
		</activity>
		
    <corollary xml:id="vid-v-to-e">
	<title>Finding E from V</title>
	
	<statement>
		<p>
			
		</p>

		<video youtube="kYJ8p1H4U3Q"><description>How to find the electric field from the electric potential.</description></video>

	</statement>
  </corollary>

  <subsubsection><title>Key Ideas</title></subsubsection>
	
	<p>Now you have seen how we can go back and forth between <m>V</m> and <m>\vec{E}</m>. To find <m>V</m> from <m>\vec{E}</m>, you can take a derivative!</p>
	
	<definition>
		<title>Determining the Electric Field from the Electric Potential</title>
		<statement>
			<p>
				
			</p>
			<p>The <term>electric field</term> can be directly calculated given a known electric potential using the equation <me>\vec{\mathit{E}} = -\vec{\nabla}\mathit{V}</me></p>
		</statement>
	</definition>

	<hypothesis xml:id="shortcuts-cartesian">
		<title>Cartesian Coordinates</title>

			<p>
				  In Cartesian coordinates, the gradient can be represented in terms of partial derivatives as:
				  <me>\vec{\mathit{E}} = -\vec{\nabla}\mathit{V} = - \frac{\partial V}{\partial x}\hat{x} - \frac{\partial V}{\partial y}\hat{y} - \frac{\partial V}{\partial z}\hat{z}</me>
			</p>
		</hypothesis>

		<subsubsection>
		<title>Activities</title>
		<activity>
      <title>Electric Field Estimate</title>
      <p></p>
			<p>Consider the <xref ref="fig_EQgraph0"/>.  Use the equation above to estimate a numerical value for the magnitude of the electric field at position <m>\vec{r} \approx (0.5 \mathrm{~m}) \hat{x}</m>.</p> 
		</activity>
	</subsubsection>

<!--NO AI-->
</section>

